  "resolution": "Dimitri Petrov was the only passenger in the sleeper cabin with the Baroness. Viktor and Charlotte were at the saloon piano, Gwen was alone at the dining bar, and Otto never left the baggage car. His gambling debts give the story its motive, but it was the snowbound seating chart that proved he was alone with her.",
  "deductions": [
    {
      "text": "The Baroness is fixed at row 5, column 1 in her sleeper cabin.",
      "clueIds": ["c3-1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Dimitri stands beside the velvet berth bed. The Baroness has the cell to its left, which leaves row 4, column 2, row 6, column 2, and row 5, column 3. Only row 4, column 2 is in row 4.",
      "clueIds": ["c3-3", "c3-4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Viktor stands beside the grand piano in the Saloon Car. Its only neighbour in row 1 is row 1, column 2.",
      "clueIds": ["c3-6", "c3-7", "c3-8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Charlotte shares the Saloon Car with Viktor and is also beside the piano, in column 3: row 2, column 3. That is a different car from Dimitri’s, as the clue says.",
      "clueIds": ["c3-2", "c3-5", "c3-9", "c3-10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Gwen has the Dining Car to herself, beside the bar counter in column 6: row 2, column 6.",
      "clueIds": ["c3-11", "c3-12", "c3-13", "c3-14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Otto is alone beside the freight crate in column 6: row 5, column 6, in the Baggage Car, a different car from Viktor.",
      "clueIds": ["c3-15", "c3-16", "c3-17", "c3-18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "With everyone placed, Dimitri is the only suspect sharing the sleeper cabin with the Baroness.",
      "clueIds": []
    }
  ],
  "helpPrompts": [
    {
      "id": "nudge-1",
      "text": "Begin with the person fixed to an exact cell.",
      "clueIds": ["c3-1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "nudge-2",
      "text": "When a clue says someone was alone, nobody else can be placed anywhere in their car.",
